# Harmonic Machines — an example PianoRules study
# This is an original demonstration of responsive-piano techniques:
# harmonic reservoirs, tremolo clouds, ostinati, phrase memory, loops and canons.
# C7 advances; C1 returns to Solo.

section Solo:
  when chord played notes 3..6 within 170ms:
    remember chord as harmony

  when any note:
    play +12 velocity input*0.18 after 900ms for 120ms

  when note C7:
    go to section Cloud

section Cloud:
  when chord played notes 3..6 within 170ms:
    morph harmony to chord over 2s

  while harmony exists every 65ms:
    play random note from harmony octave random -2..+2 velocity 14..32 for 48ms

  while harmony exists every 900ms:
    play random note from harmony range C6..C8 velocity 18..34 for 500ms

  when note C7:
    go to section Pulse

  when note C1:
    go to section Solo

section Pulse:
  when chord played notes 3..6 within 170ms:
    remember chord as harmony

  while harmony exists every 190ms:
    play next note from harmony pattern [1 3 2 4 3 2] octave -1 velocity 38 for 105ms

  while harmony exists every random 700ms..1.8s:
    play random note from harmony octave +2 velocity 18..34 for 420ms

  when note C7:
    go to section Looper

  when note C1:
    go to section Solo

section Looper:
  when phrase ends after 850ms:
    remember phrase as phrase1
    loop remembered phrase1 every 4s velocity *0.48 timing * random 0.88..1.12

  when note C7:
    go to section Canon

  when note C1:
    go to section Solo

section Canon:
  when any note:
    play +12 velocity input*0.58 after 320ms for 130ms
    play -7 velocity input*0.38 after 680ms for 160ms
    play +5 velocity input*0.24 after 1150ms for 190ms

  when phrase ends after 900ms:
    remember phrase as melody
    play remembered melody backwards transpose +12 velocity *0.42 timing *1.18

  when note C7:
    go to section Cloud

  when note C1:
    go to section Solo
